   Y ~ y0 psi^(-1/2), c ~ c0 psi^(-1/2), with [{c0: -sqrt(2)*sqrt(1/fp)/2, y0: -sqrt(2)*sqrt(fp)}, {c0: -sqrt(2)*sqrt(1/fp)/2, y0: sqrt(2)*sqrt(fp)}, {c0: sqrt(2)*sqrt(1/fp)/2, y0: -sqrt(2)*sqrt(fp)}, {c0: sqrt(2)*sqrt(1/fp)/2, y0: sqrt(2)*sqrt(fp)}]
   verdict: FAILS (movable square-root branch point; the lapse gauge c -> T'(t) c can move it, so this form
   alone is not decisive; (A) is the gauge-fixed form)

